1
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:29,980
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

2
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,980
- Birthday Party -

3
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:42,040
Hey, Sooha!

4
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,140
Welcome.

5
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:44,730
We've been waiting for you!

6
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,370
What a lovely place.

7
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:50,220
Thanks for coming.

8
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:53,290
I bet it was tough getting out here
 to the middle of the woods.

9
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:56,510
Shion's claiming he built the place.

10
00:01:56,510 --> 00:01:58,910
I mean, it's not a total lie.

11
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:04,310
We bought this place with the money 
we spent a long time saving.

12
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:05,830
True.

13
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:06,770
Sooha.

14
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:08,880
It's them.

15
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:10,760
Khan!

16
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:12,220
H-Hey.

17
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:14,260
Good to see you again.

18
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,240
Thank you for coming.

19
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,060
I'm sure the others will be glad, too.

20
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,150
What? Not really.

21
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:25,580
We only invited you to be polite, but you 
actually came. Can't you read the room?

22
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,620
So typical of you guys.

23
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:31,240
Yeah, we're here because we knew 
you'd be happy if we didn't show.

24
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,830
It was on purpose.

25
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:38,710
C-Come on. Let's go inside.

26
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:49,690
Wow!

27
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:55,070
This is my first time being 
invited to a birthday party.

28
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,940
Really?

29
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:01,020
In fact, I've never even invited 
friends to celebrate my own birthday.

30
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:05,440
So I was looking forward to 
celebrating with a large group.

31
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,340
We have games, too.

32
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:08,970
Let's have tons of fun.

33
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:09,920
Yeah!

34
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:16,400
Just so you know, 
we still don't trust you guys.

35
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,420
We don't trust you, either.

36
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:22,390
Right?

37
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:23,570
Really?

38
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:25,600
Is that true?

39
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:34,020
Happy birthday, everyone!

40
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:35,430
Thank you.

41
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,060
Thank you.

42
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:40,730
Thank you.

43
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:44,170
Happy birthday.

44
00:03:44,170 --> 00:03:46,740
Thanks, guys.

45
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:49,220
Yeah. Let's have fun today.

46
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:50,670
Tons of fun.

47
00:03:56,930 --> 00:03:58,560
Hey, uh...

48
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:00,960
About that message...

49
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,650
Oh, that? Thanks.

50
00:04:03,650 --> 00:04:06,660
What? You've been texting Sooha?

51
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:07,350
Yikes.

52
00:04:07,850 --> 00:04:10,120
Who said you could do that?

53
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:12,090
So, what'd you guys talk about?

54
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,160
This.

55
00:04:15,310 --> 00:04:18,050
A wolf cub?

56
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:21,840
You sent her a photo?

57
00:04:22,210 --> 00:04:25,800
Are you trying to get her 
attention with cute pictures?

58
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,560
You're so awkward.

59
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:30,070
See? Isn't it cute?

60
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,830
You're right! It is cute!

61
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:36,260
Send that to me, too.

62
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,540
What?!

63
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,580
Apparently, Khan loves animals.

64
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:42,990
He also sent me this, and this, and this.

65
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:44,420
Wait, wait, wait.

66
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:47,940
He doesn't love animals. He <i>is</i> an ani—

67
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:51,450
They're mostly pictures of wolf cubs, huh?

68
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:56,200
Yeah, because I like wolves.

69
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:59,440
But cats are actually my favorite.

70
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,810
Khan? Is something wrong?

71
00:05:06,570 --> 00:05:08,650
I-It's nothing.

72
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:11,450
Oh, right!

73
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:18,770
Here.

74
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,500
Happy birthday.

75
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,000
Thank you.

76
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,330
Can we open it?

77
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:27,960
Of course.

78
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:36,350
They're anti-vampire items.

79
00:05:40,610 --> 00:05:42,660
It's been so dangerous lately.

80
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:44,600
I just want you guys to be careful.

81
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:50,480
Th-Thanks. We'll treasure them.

82
00:05:53,010 --> 00:05:55,940
Wow, you've got great taste.

83
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:59,170
You're trying to protect 
them from vampire attacks?

84
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:01,290
You're so nice, Sooha.

85
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:05,210
You guys better have 
brought something, too.

86
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:08,970
Of course we did.

87
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,440
Yeah.

88
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,220
Happy birthday.

89
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:19,980
That's...

90
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,560
We've got great taste, too.

91
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:27,520
Our gifts are similar, but you can 
never have too many anti-vampire items.

92
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,960
These silver balls were expensive.

93
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,150
Here, catch.

94
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:38,660
Thanks. We'll treasure them.

95
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:43,270
This is great! You should be safe 
with this many anti-vampire items.

96
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:46,330
Y-Yeah. Thanks a lot.

97
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:49,450
That's not much of a reaction.

98
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:51,170
Can't you be happier?

99
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:55,760
Yeah. Wait, don't tell me 
you didn't like your gifts!

100
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:57,550
We're thrilled with them.

101
00:06:57,820 --> 00:06:59,800
We were just wanting something like this.

102
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,660
Good thing you chose this, Tahel.

103
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:02,760
Right?

104
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,210
Oh, really? You picked this out?

105
00:07:05,210 --> 00:07:07,250
We'll have to return the favor.

106
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:07,250
Hey, um...

107
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:09,310
Don't worry about it.

108
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,310
Here.

109
00:07:09,310 --> 00:07:12,570
Yeah, your shocked expressions 
were more than enough.

110
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,570
For me? Thank you.

111
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:14,300
We were just a little surprised.

112
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:14,300
But why?

113
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,010
We won't let it end like this.

114
00:07:14,610 --> 00:07:19,070
Uh, no reason. Open it.

115
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:17,380
Should we go buy something now?

116
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:27,360
What is this? It's so cute!

117
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,640
It's a wolf cub!

118
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:33,840
Thank you. This is the 
cutest photo I've seen.

119
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:38,220
Really? I'm glad you like it.

120
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:42,020
It's so cute.

121
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,280
Are you having fun?

122
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:51,180
What do you want?

123
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:54,990
I'm just saying hello.

124
00:07:57,010 --> 00:08:02,330
I heard your leader ran into Sooha 
on the night of the total eclipse.

125
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:03,880
Yeah.

126
00:08:04,430 --> 00:08:08,350
Is it okay for a werewolf to 
fall in love with a human girl?

127
00:08:08,350 --> 00:08:10,250
Are you really one to talk?

128
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,740
Let me make one thing clear.

129
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:15,500
I'm not like you guys.

130
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,000
What's so funny?

131
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,330
It's ironic.

132
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:23,600
That night...

133
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:30,250
you transformed like us.

134
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:35,130
Meanwhile, there are others 
who wish they could but can't.

135
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:41,910
Well, should we play a game?

136
00:08:47,130 --> 00:08:50,660
Let's start with... Werewolf!

137
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:53,170
Werewolf?

138
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:58,500
It's a game where you guess who's lying.

139
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:00,920
Really? That sounds fun.

140
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:03,890
It's perfect for this party, you know?

141
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:06,890
Let's play.

142
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,930
I'll be the game master.

143
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:11,380
Game Master: Noa

144
00:09:11,970 --> 00:09:16,420
You reside in a village where 
people live happy lives.

145
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:20,650
However, werewolves disguised 
as humans have arrived,

146
00:09:21,150 --> 00:09:23,680
and they've begun attacking
 villagers every night.

147
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:29,360
You must identify the evil werewolves 
who are deceiving the villagers.

148
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,690
Please close your eyes.

149
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,670
Werewolves, open your eyes.

150
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,720
Werewolf: Najak

151
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,720
Werewolf: Tahel

152
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,720
Ugh, you?

153
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:45,140
Werewolf: Jaan

154
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:45,140
Shut up! They'll know it's us!

155
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,920
Morning has arrived.

156
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:51,390
Everyone, please open your eyes.

157
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:54,530
Villager: Enzy

158
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:54,530
Traitor: Khan

159
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:59,280
Knight: Heli

160
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:59,280
Seer: Sooha

161
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:59,280
Villager: Solon

162
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,790
Villager: Shion

163
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,790
Villager: Jino

164
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,790
Werewolf: Jaan

165
00:10:01,830 --> 00:10:03,790
Medium: Jakah

166
00:10:03,790 --> 00:10:09,790
Now, who are the werewolves?
Discuss amongst yourselves.

167
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:12,960
It's clearly one of you guys.

168
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,010
Huh?

169
00:10:14,010 --> 00:10:15,290
Yeah.

170
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:19,290
Wait. You can't assume that yet.

171
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:21,720
Sooha, who do you think 
are the werewolves?

172
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:26,420
Who, me? Well, I think 
we'll find out at night.

173
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:28,570
Sooha, you're the seer, right?

174
00:10:28,570 --> 00:10:29,430
Yeah.

175
00:10:29,430 --> 00:10:31,540
By the way, I'm the knight.

176
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:33,320
No, you're not!

177
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,290
Are you stupid?

178
00:10:34,290 --> 00:10:35,020
Huh?

179
00:10:36,190 --> 00:10:44,880
Oh, um... that's because... 
I'm actually the knight. Yeah! That's me!

180
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:48,330
Oh, really? Then you'd better protect me.

181
00:10:48,330 --> 00:10:50,130
O-Of course I will.

182
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,580
I'm excited for tonight.

183
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,440
Y-Yeah...

184
00:10:56,370 --> 00:10:58,950
Okay, time's up.

185
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:01,930
Everyone, who do you think 
are the werewolves?

186
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,330
Point to vote.

187
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,360
Ready, and...

188
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:13,020
How'd you know?!

189
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:15,550
How could we not?

190
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:18,410
Your eyes have been darting around.

191
00:11:18,410 --> 00:11:20,610
And you've been flustered this whole time.

192
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:24,280
Why'd you guys point at me, too?

193
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:26,670
Because you put us in danger—

194
00:11:26,670 --> 00:11:28,100
Traitors!

195
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,870
Oh, that's me.

196
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:33,840
Idiot.

197
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:39,090
All right. Let's have cake.

198
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,910
Did you enjoy the party?

199
00:12:17,910 --> 00:12:21,210
Yeah. I'm glad you invited me.

200
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:24,580
I've never had this much fun before.

201
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,010
I'm glad.

202
00:12:27,010 --> 00:12:29,980
We'll have to celebrate 
your birthday next.

203
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:32,410
Really? I'd love that!

204
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:37,280
But this time, I'll host 
and invite you, Heli.

205
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:38,020
Huh?

206
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:42,190
I've never hosted a party before, though.

207
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:45,280
Okay. I'm looking forward to it.

208
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:46,730
Yeah!

209
00:12:51,170 --> 00:12:52,680
Thanks for today.

210
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:54,650
Sure. Be careful.

211
00:12:54,650 --> 00:12:56,740
You're not leaving yet?

212
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:59,920
No, we have to clean up.

213
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,670
We're staying here tonight.

214
00:13:01,670 --> 00:13:02,880
Want some help?

215
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:05,960
We'll be fine. 
Be careful on your way back.

216
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,220
Sooha!

217
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:10,140
Let's go back together.

218
00:13:12,130 --> 00:13:14,220
Well, see you at school.

219
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:16,250
Thanks for waiting.

220
00:13:22,350 --> 00:13:24,350
The food was pretty good, huh?

221
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:26,140
That was fun.

222
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:26,920
Yeah.

223
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:29,360
Would it be okay if I texted you more?

224
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:32,860
Of course. I'll look for 
things to send you, too.

225
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:38,120
<i>I forgot the present Khan gave me!</i>

226
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:41,400
Sorry, I forgot something!

227
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,520
I'll go with—

228
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:44,120
No, that's okay.

229
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:45,810
See you later.

230
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:50,510
But the sun will set soon.

231
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:55,230
I can't believe I forgot Khan's gift.

232
00:13:55,230 --> 00:13:57,510
I'd better hurry before it gets dark.

233
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:01,400
Huh?

234
00:14:05,850 --> 00:14:07,560
Where did I put it?

235
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,680
There it is.

236
00:14:12,210 --> 00:14:14,440
Maybe I'll help them after all.

237
00:14:14,890 --> 00:14:17,450
But where did they go?

238
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,610
So this is where—

239
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:47,010
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

240
00:14:47,010 --> 00:14:51,010
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

241
00:15:05,060 --> 00:15:05,800
Sooha!

242
00:15:07,310 --> 00:15:08,570
Sooha!

243
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,630
<i>Please! Hear us out!</i>

244
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:18,230
<i>Don't talk to me, creep!</i>

245
00:15:24,970 --> 00:15:25,870
Heli.

246
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:29,140
I'm going after Sooha.

247
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:30,750
What for?

248
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,340
What are you going to say?

249
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:35,930
There's nothing you can say to her now.

250
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:38,560
She saw us like this.

251
00:15:45,730 --> 00:15:47,610
But Heli...

252
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,750
What should we do now?

253
00:15:50,630 --> 00:15:52,320
There's nothing we can do.

254
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:54,900
Rumors about us will spread 
throughout the academy.

255
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:57,910
Then we'll have to run away.

256
00:15:59,410 --> 00:16:00,700
Would Sooha...

257
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:03,790
Would Sooha tell everyone?

258
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:06,560
Doesn't she hate vampires 
more than anything?

259
00:16:06,890 --> 00:16:10,000
There's no way she'd leave us alone.

260
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,300
We should start by 
talking to her in person.

261
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:15,390
Yeah! Heli, use telepathy 
to contact her first.

262
00:16:16,030 --> 00:16:19,190
When I contacted her earlier, 
she refused to listen.

263
00:16:19,690 --> 00:16:21,390
She called me a creep.

264
00:16:22,950 --> 00:16:24,430
Jakah, find her.

265
00:16:24,430 --> 00:16:25,640
Got it.

266
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:28,530
Sooha's energy is strong, 
so it shouldn't take long to...

267
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,530
A horde of vampires!

268
00:16:36,050 --> 00:16:37,950
<i>Wh-What's going on?</i>

269
00:16:37,950 --> 00:16:42,330
<i>Is Heli actually a vampire?</i>

270
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,590
<i>Not just Heli.</i>

271
00:16:44,930 --> 00:16:46,070
<i>All of them.</i>

272
00:16:53,810 --> 00:16:57,220
<i>Is that why they have those powers?</i>

273
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:03,170
You're the ones who killed 
our student, aren't you?

274
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:04,390
<i>Is that why...</i>

275
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:08,300
Could you bite my neck?

276
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:11,590
Oh, uh...

277
00:17:11,590 --> 00:17:12,550
<i>Is that why...</i>

278
00:17:12,630 --> 00:17:16,060
I-I'm not a vampire.

279
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,240
Please, believe me...

280
00:17:18,350 --> 00:17:19,490
I do.

281
00:17:19,490 --> 00:17:23,550
<i>Is that why he said 
he believed me?! But...</i>

282
00:17:24,260 --> 00:17:30,530
<i>I thought I'd finally made a friend 
who believed me since losing Chris.</i>

283
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:34,650
<i>I met friends who bore secrets like mine.</i>

284
00:17:34,650 --> 00:17:37,610
<i>I thought school was 
fun for the first time.</i>

285
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,610
<i>But it was all a lie.</i>

286
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:48,270
Heli? Did you chase after me?

287
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:52,690
S-Stay back! There's nothing
 I hate more than...

288
00:18:09,690 --> 00:18:11,700
<i>S-Someone help...</i>

289
00:18:15,310 --> 00:18:17,890
<i>Help me, Khan!</i>

290
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:21,840
Sooha?

291
00:18:33,410 --> 00:18:34,860
Sooha, are you all right?!

292
00:18:36,310 --> 00:18:37,730
I understand why you're shocked.

293
00:18:37,730 --> 00:18:40,860
But we're different from
the vampires you hate.

294
00:18:41,810 --> 00:18:43,500
Please, hear us out.

295
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:45,650
Does that mean...

296
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:49,370
Does that mean you're not a vampire?

297
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,270
And the others?

298
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:56,330
Please tell me it's not true.

299
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:58,380
That it's all a misunderstanding.

300
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:05,200
When we first met, you said you 
believed that I wasn't a vampire.

301
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:08,290
It's because you knew I wasn't one of you!

302
00:19:08,290 --> 00:19:09,900
That's why you could say that!

303
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,970
No! It's not like that!

304
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:16,270
Then why did you believe me so easily?

305
00:19:20,170 --> 00:19:21,130
Khan?

306
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,660
Ch-Chris...

307
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:30,660
Are you crying, Sooha?

308
00:19:30,990 --> 00:19:33,360
Huh? Oh, um...

309
00:19:36,430 --> 00:19:37,460
Are you okay?

310
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:43,060
I don't know what happened, 
but don't worry.

311
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:44,470
I'm here for you.

312
00:19:45,430 --> 00:19:46,700
Chris...

313
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:51,230
You're my dear friend, Sooha.

314
00:19:53,290 --> 00:19:56,500
Sooha, let's be friends.

315
00:20:00,890 --> 00:20:01,840
Okay.

316
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,380
I'm sorry I couldn't come 
see you right away.

317
00:20:07,910 --> 00:20:13,040
I was afraid you wouldn't believe 
that I'd come back to life.

318
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:16,040
I mean, it's unbelievable, right?

319
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:19,800
But I want you to believe me, Sooha.

320
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:22,820
I believe you.

321
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:26,770
Just like you believed me.

322
00:20:29,130 --> 00:20:29,950
<i>Heli!</i>

323
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:33,050
You're with Sooha, right?

324
00:20:33,050 --> 00:20:34,530
Jakah? What's going on?

325
00:20:34,530 --> 00:20:35,690
Actually, we're—

326
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:48,810
Damn it! What's going on?

327
00:20:48,810 --> 00:20:50,490
Why are there so many vampires?

328
00:20:51,030 --> 00:20:56,000
<i>Heli, I'm sensing an energy as 
powerful as Sooha's next to her.</i>

329
00:20:56,820 --> 00:20:59,000
I really missed you.

330
00:20:59,220 --> 00:21:03,260
I've spent years looking for you.

331
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:16,480
What is this?

332
00:21:18,150 --> 00:21:18,980
Sooha.

333
00:21:19,650 --> 00:21:22,610
You'll be my princess forever.

334
00:21:30,610 --> 00:21:32,660
Get away from Sooha!

335
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:41,530
You should stay out of 
this for your own sake.

336
00:21:49,250 --> 00:21:50,470
Heli...

337
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,330
Chris...

338
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:39,810
<i>Next time, Episode 7: 
"Blue Moon: That's Fate."</i>

339
00:23:36,990 --> 00:24:40,250
- That's Fate -

